---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { label: 'Editorial Standards', url: '/editorial-standards/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Standards & Fact-Checking Policy — LifeMode"
  description="LifeMode's rigorous editorial guidelines, research methodology, source verification, and transparent review processes."
  canonicalUrl="https://lifemode.life/editorial-standards/"
>
  <div class="article-container trust-page-wrapper">
    <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />

    <header class="trust-page-header">
      <span class="badge trust-badge">Transparency & Trust</span>
      <h1 class="trust-title">Editorial Standards & Fact-Checking</h1>
      <p class="trust-subtitle">
        How LifeMode researches, verifies, structures, and maintains practical household guidance.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="trust-content">
      <h2>1. Our Editorial Mission</h2>
      <p>
        LifeMode exists to provide real, actionable, and scientifically sound solutions to daily household challenges. We believe every piece of published content must be genuinely useful to a human reader—even if search engines disappeared tomorrow.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Source Hierarchy & Fact Verification</h2>
      <p>
        When making factual claims regarding food safety, temperature thresholds, chemical stain interactions, or appliance maintenance, our editorial team cross-references against authoritative primary and secondary institutions:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Food & Storage Safety:</strong> USDA Food Safety and Inspection Service (FSIS), FDA Food Code, and University Agricultural Extension Services (e.g. UC Davis, Penn State Extension).</li>
        <li><strong>Household Chemistry & Laundry:</strong> American Cleaning Institute (ACI), Textile Institute standards, and verified material safety data sheets (MSDS).</li>
        <li><strong>Home Upkeep & Preventative Care:</strong> National Fire Protection Association (NFPA), ENERGY STAR technical documentation, and certified manufacturer operational manuals.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Internal AI Usage & Quality Safeguards</h2>
      <p>
        We believe in full transparency regarding technology. AI tools may assist our research team in initial topic clustering, outline structuring, grammar QA, and formatting. However:
      </p>
      <div class="callout-box callout-tip">
        <strong>Our Technology Principle:</strong> No raw, unverified AI outputs are ever published. Every guide, metric, step, and temperature threshold is manually reviewed, fact-checked against authoritative sources, and edited for human clarity.
      </div>
      <p>We strictly prohibit automated content farming, repetitive AI filler language, and unverified statistical claims.</p>

      <h2>4. Regular Audits & Update Cycle</h2>
      <p>
        Practical standards and manufacturer guidelines evolve. We timestamp all articles with both their initial publication date and their <strong>"Last Updated & Verified"</strong> date. Our team routinely audits existing guides to ensure recommendations remain accurate and compliant with modern home standards.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Corrections & Feedback Policy</h2>
      <p>
        If you spot an error, an outdated recommendation, or have specialized insight on a household routine, we welcome corrections. Please contact our editorial desk via <a href="/contact/">our Contact Page</a> with the page URL and source reference. Verified corrections are promptly implemented.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Independence & Commercial Relationships</h2>
      <p>
        LifeMode maintains strict editorial independence. If affiliate links or sponsor relationships are introduced in the future, they will be clearly disclosed. Guides and decision recommendations are formulated entirely on functional merit, durability, and practical efficacy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .trust-page-wrapper {
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  .trust-page-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .trust-badge {
    background-color: var(--accent-emerald-light);
    color: var(--accent-emerald);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent-emerald-border);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .trust-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    color: var(--slate-950);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .trust-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--slate-600);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .trust-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .trust-content p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .trust-content ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .trust-content li {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--slate-700);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
